  "body": "for now i dont see any good way to describe for screenreaders (and also by hovering over tab icon by abled web users, same as img alt attribute) favicons in tabs and i think its a big accessibility issue, yes i know it would require some modifications in all the link tag. \r\n\r\nfor now my first idea of implementation : \r\n```\r\n<link rel=\"icon\" type=\"image/x-icon\" alt=\"icon alternative text\" href=\"image.ico\" >\r\n```\r\n\r\nand a default for alt attribute would be file name of favicon (if not specified)\r\n\r\nofcourse alt attribute would be available only with icon type of link, not as a general attribute",
